  <section class="sec__products">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-8">
          <p class="text--grey">
            <strong>Our base is located in the city of San Carlos de Bariloche, specifically Nahuel Huapi National Park in northern Patagonia.</strong> Argentina's first national park and one of its largest, Nahuel Hupai consists of an infinite number of pristine environments including both rivers and lakes. In general, the guests of Massive Trout Fly Fishing prefer to float rivers and lakes in drift boats. <strong>The season runs November to May, with opportunites to fish with dry flies or heavier sinking lines and big streamer patterns.</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            During a typical daily trip, you will be picked up by your guide at your lodging location around 08:00 am or earlier, depending on which environment we are fishing that day. We travel anywhere from 20-60 minutes until we arrive at our put-in place for fishing. Your guide will prepare the boat, the fishing equipment and provide the safety talk prior to the excursion. <strong>During the day, you can enjoy a typical water-side Argentinean lunch, with excellent wines and other beverages of your choice..</strong> If you like, you can even continue to fish while lunch is being prepared and you are enjoying a cold drink.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            Depending on the skill level of the fisherman, your guide can provide tips related specifically to fly fishing the water you are on at the time including casting techniques, floating dry flies, swinging streamers, the take, the hook set and the landing of the fish.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            <strong>Patagonia Argentina is more than rivers and lakes full of wild rainbow trout, brown and brook trout and Salmon. While fishing, we'll also see amazing native flora and fauna and wilddlife such as condors, guanacos, red deer, foxes and pumas.</strong>
            <br /><br />
            After a day of incredible fishing and sharing stories of the great catches and the ones that got away, you will finish the day around 17:00 pm. Our driver will be waiting for us as we exit the water, and your guide will take care of putting everything in order. All you need to do is think back on the day's many unforgettable moments and take another look at the photos of your amazing catches!
            <br /><br />
            What are you waiting for? Book your trip with Massive Trout Fly Fishing in order to secure the best fishing dates of the season!
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
