  <section class="sec__products">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-8">
          <p class="text--grey">
            <strong>Patagonia Argentina, is one of the few places in the world where many places remain uninhabited by humans, roads and modern noises.</strong> It is a place made of dreams, where everything one would enjoy in the outdoors comes together with Massive Trout Fly Fishing to create the ideal fishing trip, wilderness and first class comfort.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            The experience of Massive Trout Fly Fishing makes interpreting instantly what the client is looking for when planning for overnight trips. The modality of this type of trip allows our clients to fish or be in fishing environments for many more hours than daily excursions, since the days begin on the water, with a hot breakfast cooked over a fire, fishing all morning only to break for a fabulous water-side lunch and then fish the afternoon nearly to darkness before you arrive at your prepared campsite where drinks, appetizers and dinner are served and memories of the day are repeated around the crackling camp fire.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            <strong>The overnight fishing and camping environments occur in the nearest National Park, Nahuel Huapi, or Lanin National Park located 200 km northwest of the city of San Carlos de Bariloche which provide interesting options like the Rio Caleufu, Rio Collon Cura, Rio Alumine, Rio Chimehuin, and Malleo among others.</strong> The cities that are close to these environments are Junin de los Andes, San Martin de los Andes and Bariloche city.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            <strong>Usually our customers choose 3 days - 2 night overnight trips, but we can provide trips of 5 days and 4 nights. Together with the cargo boys and several 4-wheel drive trucks, we carry everything necessary for the overnight trips.</strong>
            <br /><br />
            Depending on the origin of the overnight trip, we will set out early in the morning, after your breakfast and pickup at your place of lodging. Prior to setting out, you will be provided with a dry bag (1 each two customers) of more than 60 liters where you can put everything necessary for the amount of days that will be outdoors. This bag will go into the cargo boys boat and at the end of your first day of fishing, it will be waiting for you in camp in your sleeping tent. Additionally, you will be provided a smaller bag of 20 liters for all the things you need during your day on the water that will be with you in the fishing boat.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            Once we have reached the place where we will begin the overnight trip, your guide and cargo boys put everything in order while the clients give us a hand with the assembly of the fishing equipment and even in many cases finish assembling the bags that go directly to the camp and those things that we will transport with us. After about 45 minutes of preparation, you start to float and fish, obviously after a few hours we will stop for a full lunch and drinks, with a nap in between if necessary ... there is no hurry, we have the whole river to fish! During the afternoon we will continue floating and fishing the river, taking in the magnificent scenery only to arrive around 06:00 pm to a camp already established by the cargo boys, where we will have a dinner tent, kitchen tent, our own individual tent (1 tent every two fishermen) with cots, sleeping bags, bedside table, light, pillows, and all personal items including towels to clean up after a day on the water.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            Surely the attentive cargo boys will be waiting for us with exquisite appetizers, and our drinks that you selected in the pre-trip talk. The evening will continue with a typical Argentinean dinner, all-natural beef in a grill with soft drinks, beer or wine and desserts followed by more tea or coffee if you desire.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey"><strong>In the camp you will also have your personal bathroom and if requested, a shower with warm water every night.</strong></p>
          <p class="text--grey">From here on, more days of excellent fishing, excellent service and great food awaits us!</p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            Each day the boys will move the camp around 15 - 20 km downstream, as we fish new water each day. At the end of the overnight trip, we will find the vehicles we came in that were already moved by our drivers. And, after a great group toast and "we made it", we will organize everything, to return to your place of lodging.
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey"><strong>For this kind of trip, Massive Trout Fly Fishing provides only the best camping gear necessary to experience an extraordinary outdoor experience</strong></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
          <h3>Overnight guiding rates</h3>
