  <section class="sec__products">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-8">
          <p class="text--grey">
            Many anglers prefer to choose their destination, rivers to fish and place to stay, then hire a guide service to fish. Others prefer to choose a very comfortable lodge and stay in one location and fish the waters that are there with guides that are available. Both enjoy the excellent food and cuisine that come with each. Or perhaps stall in a well-appointed hotel or apartment in downtown Bariloche and enjoy the nightlife after fishing.
            <br /><br />
            <strong>Well, there is an option. Massive Trout Fly Fishing's All-Inclusive Program</strong>
            <br /><br />
            So, let's say you are planning a one-week fishing vacation, with or without your other half or perhaps a fishing buddies' trip. You may have a designated period in the year where it all coordinates with your party. The question then becomes, where is the best fishing for that time of year? Where ever that is, where should we stay? Are there good restaurants nearby? Maybe stay at a lodge? What if we camp 1 night, stay at a lodge 2 nights and then experience the best of Bariloche's night life for 2 or 3 nights while we fish all of the days in between. How do I figure this out? Its like cherry picking the best of the best without having a clue what to do!
            <br /><br />
            <strong>Simple!</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            Let us know what you have in mind maybe as general as we just described and let us do the rest. <strong>We'll figure it all out and achieve your budget. We can also give you an option or two if you want to stretch your budget.</strong>
            <br /><br />
            There are rivers and lakes that fish excellent at certain moments and not as well other moments. There are local brew pubs in or near Bariloche with great live music and atmosphere that no tourist has ever heard of. We know where they are! How about that fabulous restaurant with the best steaks, chops or fresh trout and fabulous wine that is not a "tourist" restaurant. We know where they are and chances are, we are friends with the owner and have access to tables when they are not always available. There are lodges on certain waters that fish great at certain times of the season. Perhaps stay 2 nights, fish 2 or 3 days, have the fine lodging experience, then change it up for 2 nights camping and floating, then hit the town for 2 nights for the bon voyage back to reality! While fishing every day in between if your arm doesn't fall off!
          </p>
          <p class="text--grey"><strong>Massive Trout Fly Fishing All-Inclusive Plan is an awesome way to do it all when you have no idea how to do it!</strong></p>
          <p class="text--grey">
            <strong>You can reference our all-inclusive rates for costs which include lodging in hotels or apartments in or near Bariloche. Our all-inclusive rates exclude rates for Lodges outside the town of Bariloche. Depending on the time of season, availability and number of people in a reservation, we will request and provide rates from Lodges requested by our Guests.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
